  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical assistence e-certification Colombia National Institute for Food and Drug Surveillance (INVIMA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the Free Trade Agreement between the EU and Colombia in 2013, the export of agricultural products from Colombia to the EU has increased by 38%. Colombia still uses paper certificates, a process prone to lengthy procedures and potential fraud. The introduction of e-certification will lead to more (time) efficient import and export procedures as it reduces the time inspectors spend on the certification process, reduces the chances of fraud, eases the process to reduce mistakes that have been made and reduces the time that is needed to examine the certificates. Together with INVIMA (Colombian Competent Authority for Food and Medicines), such an e-certification process will be designed, tested and implemented.</narrative>
  </description>
